      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a one-time validation task (exercising a test merge) completed before an operational change, not an ongoing system property"
      },
      "user_decision": "accept",
      "post_migration_section": "CC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "This project's dso-config.conf updated: enforcement.strategy=ci. Pre-commit hooks and PreToolUse hooks emit HOOK_GATE: skipped reason=enforcement.strategy=ci on subsequent commits \u2014 verified in-session by inspecting one commit's hook output.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "the configuration file update and resulting hook behavior represent durable system properties that persist beyond the initial change"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "Deliberate test PR opened that violates a rule the local gate previously caught (e.g., a critical security finding the security overlay should catch); CI-side enforcement (Ruleset checks via epic 5d6e-86a9's parity-uplifted llm-review plus the Ruleset's required-checks list) blocks merge \u2014 verified in-session via gh pr checks showing the failed check and gh pr merge --auto queued but not executing.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a one-time verification task (opening a test PR and confirming CI blocks it) rather than an ongoing system property"
      },
      "user_decision": "accept",
      "post_migration_section": "CC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "After the deliberate-violation PR confirms the CI block, the PR is closed without merging and its branch deleted in the same session \u2014 verified in-session via gh pr view --state all showing state CLOSED.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 5,
        "rationale": "describes a one-time verification task with explicit completion criteria (PR closed, branch deleted, verified in session)"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "CC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "Plugin scripts whose only consumers are the now-dormant local enforcement path identified via a Part C downstream-consumer scan using grep -rn against plugins/dso/skills/, plugins/dso/scripts/, plugins/dso/hooks/, and tests/ for each candidate script's filename; the scan produces an explicit candidate list; every script on the list is either deleted in this epic's commit OR annotated with the non-enforcement consumer that keeps it alive. The list may be empty if no scripts qualify \u2014 that is an acceptable outcome.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a one-time task of identifying and either deleting or annotating scripts based on a specific scan outcome, not an ongoing system property"
      },
      "user_decision": "reject",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    }
  ]
